.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt NDPKG 8
.Os NeoDarwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndpkg
.Nd NeoDarwin package manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r Ar repo ...
.Cm install | remove | upgrade
.Op Fl -json
.Ar package ...
.Nm
.Op Fl r Ar repo ...
.Cm plan
.Cm install | remove | upgrade
.Ar package ...
.Nm
.Cm apply
.Ar plan.json
.Nm
.Cm list | info
.Op Fl -json
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm index
.Ar dir
.Nm
.Cm activate | gc
.Nm
.Cm activate-trust
.Ar file.ndpkg
.Nm
.Cm load-trust
.Ar module grant
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs, upgrades and removes signed
.Pa .ndpkg
packages under
.Pa /usr/local .
Every package is verified against the package roots the kernel trusts
(the
.Va nd_pkg_root
boot argument): its manifest's signature, its trust cache and every
payload file.
A verified package is unpacked into a content-addressed, read-only store
entry,
.Pa /var/db/ndpkg/store/ Ns Ar payload-sha256 Ns - Ns Ar name Ns - Ns Ar version ,
which is mounted read-only and nosuid with nullfs at
.Pa /var/db/ndpkg/mnt/ Ns Ar entry ;
.Pa /var/db/ndpkg/active/ Ns Ar name
links to the mounted tree, and
.Pa /usr/local
holds one symbolic link per package file into it.
An upgrade moves the
.Pa active
link, so the files change in one rename.
.Pp
Dependencies are solved with libsolv over the installed packages and the
repositories: the
.Fl r
directories, or the lines of
.Pa /etc/ndpkg/repositories .
A repository is a directory of packages and the
.Pa index.json
that
.Cm index
writes.
Package arguments are names,
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar version ,
or, for
.Cm install ,
package files.
.Cm plan
prints the transaction as JSON without changing anything;
.Cm apply
executes such a plan if the installed state is still the generation it
names.
.Cm install ,
.Cm remove
and
.Cm upgrade
plan and apply at once;
.Cm upgrade
without names upgrades everything.
.Pp
.Cm activate
makes the installed state live again after a boot: it reloads the
packages' trust caches, mounts their entries and restores their links.
.Cm gc
removes store entries that neither the installed state nor the previous
generation refers to.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /var/db/ndpkg/installed
the installed state: a link to
.Pa generations/ Ns Ar N ,
which holds
.Ar name Ns Pa /manifest ,
.Pa files
and
.Pa state
for each package
.It Pa /var/db/ndpkg/store
verified packages, read-only
.It Pa /etc/ndpkg/repositories
repository directories, one per line
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NeoDarwin's P2-01 (trust caches) and P2-02 (the store,
solver and plans).
